:: Water Collection Facility {"position":"600,600","size":"100,100"}
<img src="https://i.postimg.cc/8C0GwKyg/d.png" alt="Starting Image" style="display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;">

The Water Collection Facility stands as one of the most intact structures in Eagar, its utilitarian design having weathered the years better than most buildings. Large cisterns on the roof connect to an array of pipes and filtration systems. This was clearly vital infrastructure during the water scarcity that followed climate collapse.

The main entrance is secured but can be forced open with effort. Inside, you find a control room with offline monitoring systems, an administrative area with terminals, storage spaces for maintenance equipment, and access to an underground cistern.

The facility has been abandoned for decades, but its robust construction means some systems might still be salvageable—or at least contain valuable parts or information.

[[Check the control room|Search the control room]] - Examine the facility's operational center.
[[Try the computer terminal|Access computer terminal]] - Attempt to retrieve data from the administrative systems.
